       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That's more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day (many hospitals use 3,000 mg/day or less). A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the typical 1,000 mg maximum. Doses like this risk serious liver toxicity, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1,000 mg by mouth three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **3,000 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me which you want, or give me a different dose, and I'll enter it right away. Please also review the order with your supervising resident or attending, and check that the patient isn't getting acetaminophen from other sources, such as combination products."
